# The descriptor is written at the call and lays a value that is read only: on an object in sight the value lies under the name from then on, as behind a store, and does not go to unseen code. L0 = what is laid, L2 = the object. What is stored on made.inner is followed: the arrow function is the only thing under `run`.
# RUN: link fields mechanisms=all
# CHECK: field L0.2 "run" appended proven=f2 writers-known
# CHECK: field L2.0 "inner" proven=L0 writers-known
